#* {{quote-book|en|title=The antiquary |author=Walter Scott |year=1836 |page=56 |passage=I dinna ken,” said Steenie ; “ the book had fa'en out 0' his pocket, I fancy, for I fand it amang my feet when I was '''graping''' about to set him on his legs again, and I just pat it in my pouch to keep it safe ; }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Two Lawyers |author=Robert Burns |year=1881 |page=280 |passage='Till in a declamation mist, His argument he tint it; He gapéd for't, he '''graped''' for't, He fand it was awa, man; }}
